{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WWHg4W3M8pAX75XScm58Di","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Docker-Mailserver Project\n2\t\n3\t> 🔀 **Session history (refocus)**: See [docs/refocus/INDEX.md](docs/refocus/INDEX.md) for incoming briefs and outbound spawns.\n4\t\n5\t## Current Status (2026-07-28): AWS edge live, MX not yet cut over\n6\t\n7\tThe stack was rebuilt behind an AWS edge (`~/projects/aws/mail-edge/`, Elastic IP\n8\t`34.194.247.228`) because Verizon residential blocks inbound port 25 and lacks IP reputation\n9\tfor outbound delivery. See [`docs/aws-edge-integration.md`](docs/aws-edge-integration.md) for\n10\tthe full design, verified log evidence, and open items — this section is the summary.\n11\t\n12\t- `mailserver` and `mail-edge-wg` (containerized WireGuard peer) are both **up and healthy**.\n13\t  `mailserver` joins `mail-edge-wg`'s network namespace via `network_mode:\n14\t  service:mail-edge-wg` — it has no `networks:`/`ports:`/Traefik labels of its own; restarting\n15\t  `mail-edge-wg` destroys that namespace and requires restarting `mailserver` afterward.\n16\t- PROXY protocol (HAProxy v2) is configured on Postfix (`config/postfix-master.cf`, scoped\n17\t  per-listener) and Dovecot (`config/dovecot.cf`, `haproxy_trusted_networks = 10.77.0.1/32`)\n18\t  for all four edge-forwarded ports: 25, 465, 587, 993. **Verified working** — DMS logs show\n19\t  the real client IP end-to-end, not the tunnel peer's.\n20\t- **MX for `ai-servicers.com` still points at Cloudflare Email Routing.** No production mail\n21\t  flows through this edge yet; cutover is a deliberate, separate human decision (not\n22\t  automated). `mail.ai-servicers.com` currently resolves to the Elastic IP with Cloudflare's\n23\t  proxy off, and was removed from `ddns-updater` so nothing overwrites it.\n24\t- The Elastic IP's PTR record is still **pending** at AWS — do not send test mail to\n25\t  third-party domains (Gmail, Outlook, etc.) until it resolves.\n26\t- 🔴 **Regression: Traefik's TCP routing to mail is currently broken**, and with it internal\n27\t  clients that relied on it (e.g. Nextcloud Mail at `mail.ai-servicers.com:993`/`:587`).\n28\t  Traefik discovered mail routers from Docker labels on the old `mailserver` container;\n29\t  `network_mode: service:*` forbids labels on the new one, so those routers no longer exist.\n30\t  Confirmed: `mail.ai-servicers.com:993` now TLS-handshakes then returns"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30","uuid":"99aa7a96-c218-40ca-a2fd-47759d881bc0","timestamp":"2026-07-28T22:19:12.952Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/CLAUDE.md","content":"# Docker-Mailserver Project\n\n> 🔀 **Session history (refocus)**: See [docs/refocus/INDEX.md](docs/refocus/INDEX.md) for incoming briefs and outbound spawns.\n\n## Current Status (2026-07-28): AWS edge live, MX not yet cut over\n\nThe stack was rebuilt behind an AWS edge (`~/projects/aws/mail-edge/`, Elastic IP\n`34.194.247.228`) because Verizon residential blocks inbound port 25 and lacks IP reputation\nfor outbound delivery. See [`docs/aws-edge-integration.md`](docs/aws-edge-integration.md) for\nthe full design, verified log evidence, and open items — this section is the summary.\n\n- `mailserver` and `mail-edge-wg` (containerized WireGuard peer) are both **up and healthy**.\n  `mailserver` joins `mail-edge-wg`'s network namespace via `network_mode:\n  service:mail-edge-wg` — it has no `networks:`/`ports:`/Traefik labels of its own; restarting\n  `mail-edge-wg` destroys that namespace and requires restarting `mailserver` afterward.\n- PROXY protocol (HAProxy v2) is configured on Postfix (`config/postfix-master.cf`, scoped\n  per-listener) and Dovecot (`config/dovecot.cf`, `haproxy_trusted_networks = 10.77.0.1/32`)\n  for all four edge-forwarded ports: 25, 465, 587, 993. **Verified working** — DMS logs show\n  the real client IP end-to-end, not the tunnel peer's.\n- **MX for `ai-servicers.com` still points at Cloudflare Email Routing.** No production mail\n  flows through this edge yet; cutover is a deliberate, separate human decision (not\n  automated). `mail.ai-servicers.com` currently resolves to the Elastic IP with Cloudflare's\n  proxy off, and was removed from `ddns-updater` so nothing overwrites it.\n- The Elastic IP's PTR record is still **pending** at AWS — do not send test mail to\n  third-party domains (Gmail, Outlook, etc.) until it resolves.\n- 🔴 **Regression: Traefik's TCP routing to mail is currently broken**, and with it internal\n  clients that relied on it (e.g. Nextcloud Mail at `mail.ai-servicers.com:993`/`:587`).\n  Traefik discovered mail routers from Docker labels on the old `mailserver` container;\n  `network_mode: service:*` forbids labels on the new one, so those routers no longer exist.\n  Confirmed: `mail.ai-servicers.com:993` now TLS-handshakes then returns","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":276}}}
