{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LSujUUSV3qgFKfQTEfmzaK","type":"tool_result","content":"30\t  Confirmed: `mail.ai-servicers.com:993` now TLS-handshakes then returns\n31\t  `HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request` instead of proxying IMAP. See \"Traefik TCP Routing\" below and\n32\t  `docs/aws-edge-integration.md` for detail. Fixing this is a Traefik-project change, not done\n33\t  here.\n34\t\n35\t### Mail Accounts\n36\t- **websurfinmurf@ai-servicers.com** - Active and working\n37\t- **michaelmurphy@ai-servicers.com** - Configured (legacy)\n38\t\n39\t### SSL Configuration\n40\t- **Type**: manual\n41\t- **Certificates**: Let's Encrypt via Traefik\n42\t- **Path**: `/certs/certificate.crt` and `/certs/privatekey.key`\n43\t- **Mount**: `/home/administrator/projects/data/traefik-certs/ai-servicers.com:/certs:ro`\n44\t\n45\t## Architecture\n46\t- **Container**: ghcr.io/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver:latest, joined to\n47\t  `mail-edge-wg`'s netns (see Current Status above) — no direct `mailserver-net`/`traefik-net`\n48\t  attachment of its own.\n49\t- **WireGuard peer**: `mail-edge-wg` (`lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard`), dials out to the AWS\n50\t  edge at `34.194.247.228:51820`; tunnel addresses `10.77.0.1` (edge) / `10.77.0.2` (home).\n51\t- **Management UI**: PostfixAdmin at postfixadmin.ai-servicers.com\n52\t- **Database**: PostgreSQL (shared instance) for PostfixAdmin\n53\t- **Networks**: `mailserver-net` (mail-edge-wg, postfixadmin), `traefik-net` (postfixadmin only)\n54\t\n55\t## Configuration Files\n56\t- `$HOME/projects/secrets/docker-mailserver.env` - Main environment configuration\n57\t- `$HOME/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` - WireGuard peer config (mode 600)\n58\t- `config/postfix-accounts.cf` - Account configuration (managed by setup command)\n59\t- `config/postfix-virtual.cf` - Virtual aliases configuration\n60\t- `config/postfix-master.cf` - PROXY protocol overrides (Postfix side)\n61\t- `config/dovecot.cf` - PROXY protocol overrides (Dovecot side)\n62\t\n63\t## Key Environment Settings\n64\t```env\n65\tHOSTNAME=mail\n66\tDOMAINNAME=ai-servicers.com\n67\tPERMIT_DOCKER=network\n68\tSSL_TYPE=manual\n69\tSSL_CERT_PATH=/certs/certificate.crt\n70\tSSL_KEY_PATH=/certs/privatekey.key\n71\tTLS_LEVEL=intermediate\n72\tENABLE_SPAMASSASSIN=1\n73\tENABLE_FAIL2BAN=1\n74\tENABLE_POSTGREY=1\n75\t```\n76\t\n77\t## Network Configuration\n78\t- Connected to three networks for full integration:\n79\t  - `mailserver-net` - Primary network\n80\t  - `traefik-net` - For external access via Traefik\n81\t  - `postgres-net` - For PostfixAdmin database access\n82\t- Postfix configured to trust Docker networks: `172.16.0.0/12 10.0.0.0/8`\n83\t\n84\t## Deployment Scripts"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30","uuid":"03063c19-fcb5-4ed0-a779-22b4b99ec2f2","timestamp":"2026-07-28T22:19:18.037Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/CLAUDE.md","content":"  Confirmed: `mail.ai-servicers.com:993` now TLS-handshakes then returns\n  `HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request` instead of proxying IMAP. See \"Traefik TCP Routing\" below and\n  `docs/aws-edge-integration.md` for detail. Fixing this is a Traefik-project change, not done\n  here.\n\n### Mail Accounts\n- **websurfinmurf@ai-servicers.com** - Active and working\n- **michaelmurphy@ai-servicers.com** - Configured (legacy)\n\n### SSL Configuration\n- **Type**: manual\n- **Certificates**: Let's Encrypt via Traefik\n- **Path**: `/certs/certificate.crt` and `/certs/privatekey.key`\n- **Mount**: `/home/administrator/projects/data/traefik-certs/ai-servicers.com:/certs:ro`\n\n## Architecture\n- **Container**: ghcr.io/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver:latest, joined to\n  `mail-edge-wg`'s netns (see Current Status above) — no direct `mailserver-net`/`traefik-net`\n  attachment of its own.\n- **WireGuard peer**: `mail-edge-wg` (`lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard`), dials out to the AWS\n  edge at `34.194.247.228:51820`; tunnel addresses `10.77.0.1` (edge) / `10.77.0.2` (home).\n- **Management UI**: PostfixAdmin at postfixadmin.ai-servicers.com\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL (shared instance) for PostfixAdmin\n- **Networks**: `mailserver-net` (mail-edge-wg, postfixadmin), `traefik-net` (postfixadmin only)\n\n## Configuration Files\n- `$HOME/projects/secrets/docker-mailserver.env` - Main environment configuration\n- `$HOME/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` - WireGuard peer config (mode 600)\n- `config/postfix-accounts.cf` - Account configuration (managed by setup command)\n- `config/postfix-virtual.cf` - Virtual aliases configuration\n- `config/postfix-master.cf` - PROXY protocol overrides (Postfix side)\n- `config/dovecot.cf` - PROXY protocol overrides (Dovecot side)\n\n## Key Environment Settings\n```env\nHOSTNAME=mail\nDOMAINNAME=ai-servicers.com\nPERMIT_DOCKER=network\nSSL_TYPE=manual\nSSL_CERT_PATH=/certs/certificate.crt\nSSL_KEY_PATH=/certs/privatekey.key\nTLS_LEVEL=intermediate\nENABLE_SPAMASSASSIN=1\nENABLE_FAIL2BAN=1\nENABLE_POSTGREY=1\n```\n\n## Network Configuration\n- Connected to three networks for full integration:\n  - `mailserver-net` - Primary network\n  - `traefik-net` - For external access via Traefik\n  - `postgres-net` - For PostfixAdmin database access\n- Postfix configured to trust Docker networks: `172.16.0.0/12 10.0.0.0/8`\n\n## Deployment Scripts","numLines":55,"startLine":30,"totalLines":276}}}
