{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gubzk8g5LGHPHeje6UNxXc","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t```bash\n151\tcd /home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver\n152\t./apply-relay.sh  # Reads from docker-mailserver.env\n153\t```\n154\t\n155\t## Integration with Nextcloud\n156\t\n157\t### 🔴 Currently broken (2026-07-28) — see Current Status above\n158\tNextcloud Mail previously connected via `mail.ai-servicers.com:993`/`:587` through Traefik's\n159\tTCP passthrough. That path is confirmed dead now that `mailserver` carries no Docker labels\n160\t(`network_mode: service:*` forbids them) — Traefik has no router to send it to. This section\n161\tdescribes the *previously working* configuration, kept for reference; it is not currently\n162\tfunctional and needs a Traefik-side fix (new label source, or a file-provider route to\n163\t`mail-edge-wg`) that is out of scope for the edge/tunnel work described above.\n164\t\n165\tNextcloud Mail app previously connected using:\n166\t- **Server**: mail.ai-servicers.com\n167\t- **IMAP**: Port 993 with SSL\n168\t- **SMTP**: Port 587 with STARTTLS\n169\t- **Authentication**: Username/password from setup command\n170\t- **Outbound**: Relayed through SendGrid for deliverability\n171\t\n172\t### NAT Reflection Workaround\n173\tDue to ASUS router NAT reflection, Nextcloud container has:\n174\t- External DNS servers (8.8.8.8) configured\n175\t- Hosts entry mapping mail.ai-servicers.com → 172.22.0.17\n176\t- This allows internal Docker routing while using external domain name\n177\t\n178\t## Traefik TCP Routing — 🔴 broken, not currently in effect\n179\tPreviously all mail ports were routed through Traefik with TLS passthrough via Docker labels"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30","uuid":"7d34632a-b8b8-4d29-bf8b-2044262a16f5","timestamp":"2026-07-28T22:19:48.665Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/CLAUDE.md","content":"```bash\ncd /home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver\n./apply-relay.sh  # Reads from docker-mailserver.env\n```\n\n## Integration with Nextcloud\n\n### 🔴 Currently broken (2026-07-28) — see Current Status above\nNextcloud Mail previously connected via `mail.ai-servicers.com:993`/`:587` through Traefik's\nTCP passthrough. That path is confirmed dead now that `mailserver` carries no Docker labels\n(`network_mode: service:*` forbids them) — Traefik has no router to send it to. This section\ndescribes the *previously working* configuration, kept for reference; it is not currently\nfunctional and needs a Traefik-side fix (new label source, or a file-provider route to\n`mail-edge-wg`) that is out of scope for the edge/tunnel work described above.\n\nNextcloud Mail app previously connected using:\n- **Server**: mail.ai-servicers.com\n- **IMAP**: Port 993 with SSL\n- **SMTP**: Port 587 with STARTTLS\n- **Authentication**: Username/password from setup command\n- **Outbound**: Relayed through SendGrid for deliverability\n\n### NAT Reflection Workaround\nDue to ASUS router NAT reflection, Nextcloud container has:\n- External DNS servers (8.8.8.8) configured\n- Hosts entry mapping mail.ai-servicers.com → 172.22.0.17\n- This allows internal Docker routing while using external domain name\n\n## Traefik TCP Routing — 🔴 broken, not currently in effect\nPreviously all mail ports were routed through Traefik with TLS passthrough via Docker labels","numLines":30,"startLine":150,"totalLines":291}}}
