{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdVEhTsSJQCnbAD9mjCgh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WTHq48nN7dUg7gqJRB5VV3","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/refocus/2026-07-28-mail-cert-san-59a355.md","old_string":"## Result\n<empty until child writes>\n","new_string":"## Result\n\n**Status**: completed\n\n**Definition-of-Done met**\n- ✓ `docker exec mailserver openssl x509 -in /etc/dms/tls/cert -noout -ext subjectAltName` → `DNS:*.ai-servicers.com, DNS:ai-servicers.com`.\n- ✓ Peer-verified TLS to `mail.ai-servicers.com:993` succeeds — checked with hostname\n  verification actually enabled (`-verify_hostname mail.ai-servicers.com`, not just chain\n  trust), and a negative control (`-verify_hostname nope.example.com`) confirmed the flag\n  rejects a mismatched name, proving the positive check was real. Also confirmed SMTP 587\n  (`Verified peername: *.ai-servicers.com`) since Nextcloud Mail needs both.\n- ✓ `mailserver` and `mail-edge-wg` both `healthy` after restarting only `mailserver` (per the\n  brief's gotcha, `mail-edge-wg` was left untouched). Port 25 through the edge answers\n  `220 mail.ai-servicers.com ESMTP`.\n- ✓ Change and both gotchas recorded in `CLAUDE.md` (SSL Configuration section + an update\n  note under Integration with Nextcloud).\n\n**Summary**\n`mailserver`'s cert bind mount pointed at Traefik's apex-only `ai-servicers.com` cert dir\n(SAN `ai-servicers.com` only). Repointed it at the wildcard dir\n(`*.ai-servicers.com`, SAN `*.ai-servicers.com, ai-servicers.com`) in `docker-compose.yml`,\nquoted for YAML safety per the brief's glob-character gotcha. Restarted only `mailserver`;\nboth containers came back healthy. Verified with a genuine hostname-verifying TLS handshake\n(not just chain trust) against the public edge IP with SNI `mail.ai-servicers.com`, on both\n993 and 587. Traefik's cert extraction was untouched, confirming the brief's diagnosis that\nit was never at fault.\n\n**Artifacts produced**\n- `docker-compose.yml` — cert bind-mount source changed to the wildcard directory.\n- `CLAUDE.md` — SSL Configuration section rewritten with the fix, rationale, and both\n  gotchas (glob-char directory name; traefik-certs dir is write-denied, inspect read-only via\n  `docker exec`); Nextcloud integration section updated with a 2026-07-28 note distinguishing\n  this (now-fixed) cert blocker from the still-open Traefik LAN routing regression.\n- Commit `34ba745` on `main`, pushed to `origin/main`.\n\n**Suggested follow-ups (parent decides)**\n- Divergent uncommitted WIP was found already in this working tree at start of session,\n  unrelated to this brief, and deliberately left untouched (staged only my own hunks via\n  `git add -p`): a `192.168.1.13:143:143` port mapping on `mail-edge-wg` in\n  `docker-compose.yml`, and catch-all aliases in `config/postfix-virtual.cf`\n  (`@ai-servicers.com`, `hello@ai-servicers.com` → `websurfinmurf@ai-servicers.com`). These\n  look like leftover work from the sibling `2026-07-28-proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077` session\n  (its `.worker.log` is also modified, uncommitted). Because I recreated `mailserver` via\n  `docker compose up -d mailserver`, it re-read the bind-mounted `./config`, so the\n  uncommitted `postfix-virtual.cf` aliases (including the `@ai-servicers.com` catch-all) are\n  now **live in the running Postfix**, uncommitted, with MX pointing at this server. The\n  `proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077` session (or its parent) should review and commit or discard\n  this WIP.\n- Untracked `docker-compose.yml.bak-lan143` in the repo root — appears to be a manual backup\n  from other WIP, not mine; left alone.\n- The still-open Traefik LAN TCP-routing regression (`mail.ai-servicers.com:993` via\n  `192.168.1.13` returns `HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request`) is unrelated to this fix and remains a\n  Traefik-project change, per existing CLAUDE.md.\n\n**Material changes (for /context-save)**\n- `docs/context/security.md` (or equivalent): the mail TLS certificate source changed from\n  the apex-only Traefik-dumped dir to the wildcard dir, fixing SAN validation for\n  `mail.ai-servicers.com` — update if a canonical cert-path fact lives there.\n- No architecture-level change (same cert source, same dumper, same container topology) —\n  primarily a bind-mount source correction.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264,"cache_read_input_tokens":103757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30","uuid":"163d6176-8cc2-4f16-ac36-6ce6062e5f9f","timestamp":"2026-07-28T22:23:04.427Z","request_id":"req_011CdVEhSRsQpWmq2xgfNz4a"}
