lob-character gotcha. Restarted only `mailserver`;\nboth containers came back healthy. Verified with a genuine hostname-verifying TLS handshake\n(not just chain trust) against the public edge IP with SNI `mail.ai-servicers.com`, on both\n993 and 587. Traefik's cert extraction was untouched, confirming the brief's diagnosis that\nit was never at fault.\n\n**Artifacts produced**\n- `docker-compose.yml` — cert bind-mount source changed to the wildcard directory.\n- `CLAUDE.md` — SSL Configuration section rewritten with the fix, rationale, and both\n  gotchas (glob-char directory name; traefik-certs dir is write-denied, inspect read-only via\n  `docker exec`); Nextcloud integration section updated with a 2026-07-28 note distinguishing\n  this (now-fixed) cert blocker from the still-open Traefik LAN routing regression.\n- Commit `34ba745` on `main`, pushed to `origin/main`.\n\n**Suggested follow-ups (parent decides)**\n- Divergent uncommitted WIP was found already in this working tree at start of session,\n  unrelated to this brief, and deliberately left untouched (staged only my own hunks via\n  `git add -p`): a `192.168.1.13:143:143` port mapping on `mail-edge-wg` in\n  `docker-compose.yml`, and catch-all aliases in `config/postfix-virtual.cf`\n  (`@ai-servicers.com`, `hello@ai-servicers.com` → `websurfinmurf@ai-servicers.com`). These\n  look like leftover work from the sibling `2026-07-28-proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077` session\n  (its `.worker.log` is also modified, uncommitted). Because I recreated `mailserver` via\n  `docker compose up -d mailserver`, it re-read the bind-mounted `./config`, so the\n  uncommitted `postfix-virtual.cf` aliases (including the `@ai-servicers.com` catch-all) are\n  now **live in the running Postfix**, uncommitted, with MX pointing at this server. The\n  `proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077` session (or its parent) should review and commit or discard\n  this WIP.\n- Untracked `docker-compose.yml.bak-lan143` in the repo root — appears to be a manual backup\n  from other WIP, not mine; left alone.\n- The still-open Traefik LAN TCP-routing regression (`mail.ai-servicers.com:993` via\n  `192.168.1.13` returns `HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request`) is unrelated to this fix and remains a\n  Traefik-project change, per existing CLAUDE.md.\n\n**Material changes (for /context-save)**\n- `docs/context/security.md` (or equivalent): the mail TLS certificate source changed from\n  the apex-only Traefik-dumped dir to the wildcard dir, fixing SAN validation for\n  `mail.ai-servicers.com` — update if a canonical cert-path fact lives there.\n- No architecture-level change (same cert source, same dumper, same container topology) —\n  primarily a bind-mount source correction.\n","originalFile":"---\nid: 2026-07-28-mail-cert-san-59a355\nstatus: result\nchild_session_id: 59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30\nspawn_mode: execute\ntier: low\nspawned_at: 2026-07-28T15:20:00Z\nlaunched_at: 2026-07-28T22:16:27Z\ncompleted_at: 2026-07-28T22:55:00Z\nsource_dir: /home/administrator/projects/aws\nsource_session_id: 700184f3-55a6-4052-b9fa-225f8550bc2e\ndest_dir: /home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver\nslug: mail-cert-san\nparent_refocus_id: 2026-07-28-proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077\nrelated_refocus_ids: []\ndone_when:\n  - \"docker exec mailserver openssl x509 -in /etc/dms/tls/cert -noout -ext subjectAltName includes mail.ai-servicers.com (via the *.ai-servicers.com wildcard).\"\n  - \"A TLS connection to mail.ai-servicers.com:993 validates with peer verification ON — the exact condition Nextcloud Mail requires.\"\n  - \"mailserver and mail-edge-wg are both healthy afterwards, and port 25 through the AWS edge (34.194.247.228) still answers 220.\"\n  - \"The bind-mount change and its reason are recorded in CLAUDE.md.\"\nout_of_scope:\n  - \"Do NOT modify Traefik, traefik-certs-dumper, or acme.json. The extraction is CORRECT — it already writes both certificates. Nothing there is broken.\"\n  - \"Do NOT write to the traefik-certs directory under the platform data tree. It is hard-denied by the destructive-guard hook. Reference it from the compose file only; inspect it read-only via `docker exec` into a container that already mounts it.\"\n  - \"Do NOT disable TLS peer verification anywhere, in Nextcloud or elsewhere. That converts the symptom into a silent security hole.\"\n  - \"Do NOT change MX records, any DNS, or anything in ~/projects/aws.\"\n  - \"Do NOT touch Nextcloud. Deleting or repointing Mail account id 3 belongs to the projects/nextcloud session.\"\nrelated: []\n---\n\n# Brief: serve the wildcard cert so mail.ai-servicers.com validates\n\n## Why this branch exists\nNextcloud Mail cannot open IMAP: `mailserver` presents a certificate whose only SAN is\n`ai-servicers.com`, so validating clients reject `mail.ai-servicers.com`. The\n`projects/nextcloud` session diagnosed the symptom correctly but concluded Traefik's\ncertificate extraction was faulty. It is not. The dumper writes **both** certificates into\nseparate directories; `docker-mailserver` simply bind-mounts the wrong one. The fix is one\nline here, and Traefik needs no change at all.\n\n## Inherited context\n- `traefik-certs-dumper` runs `file --version v3 --domain-subdir --source /traefik/acme.json\n  --dest /certs --watch`, producing one directory per certificate.\n- Verified contents of that output directory (read-only, via `docker exec` into the dumper):\n  - `*.ai-servicers.com/` → `certificate.crt`, `privatekey.key`  ← **the wildcard, what we want**\n  - `ai-servicers.com/`   → `certificate.crt`, `privatekey.key`  ← apex-only, what we serve today\n  - plus `diagrams.nginx.…`, `registry.gitlab.…`, and `private/letsencrypt.key`\n- `acme.json` holds 4 certificates including **separate** `ai-servicers.com` and\n  `*.ai-servicers.com` entries. Both are legitimately issued; this is not a mis-issuance.\n- `mailserver` is `SSL_TYPE=manual`, `SSL_CERT_PATH=/certs/certificate.crt`,\n  `SSL_KEY_PATH=/certs/privatekey.key`. Its certificate bind mount currently targets the\n  **`ai-servicers.com`** subdirectory.\n- Confirmed served SAN today: `DNS:ai-servicers.com` only. Confirmed wildcard on Traefik's\n  `:443`: `DNS:*.ai-servicers.com, DNS:ai-servicers.com`.\n- **Gotcha:** the target directory is literally named `*.ai-servicers.com`. A glob character\n  in a path. Quote it correctly in YAML and in any shell command, or it will silently expand\n  or fail to match.\n- **Gotcha:** restarting `mail-edge-wg` kills `mailserver` with exit 128 — `mailserver` uses\n  `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg` and loses the namespace. Recovery is\n  `docker compose up -d mailserver`. Restarting `mailserver` alone is safe and is all this\n  change needs.\n- **MX now points at this server.** Mail is live and no longer forwards to Gmail, so downtime\n  during this change is real lost mail, not a lab inconvenience. Keep the restart tight.\n- Nextcloud reaches IMAP only through the public `34.194.247.228:993` — its container resolver\n  returns the AWS Elastic IP, not the LAN address. The certificate must therefore validate on\n  the public path; a LAN-only fix does not help it.\n- Ports 25/465/587/993 all mandate PROXY protocol (`haproxy_trusted_networks = 10.77.0.1/32`).\n  Port 143 is plain and published LAN-only on `192.168.1.13`. Use 143 for local probes; use the\n  edge for the validating probe.\n\n## Open questions / desired deliverables\n- Point the certificate bind mount at the wildcard directory and restart `mailserver`.\n- Prove the served certificate now covers `mail.ai-servicers.com`.\n- Prove a peer-verifying TLS client succeeds against `mail.ai-servicers.com:993` — that is the\n  precise condition Nextcloud Mail needs, and the reason this work exists.\n- Decide whether to reference the wildcard directory directly or via a stable symlink or an\n  `SSL_CERT_PATH` change; pick one and record why. A directory containing a glob character is a\n  foot-gun for whoever edits this next.\n- Record the change and both gotchas above in `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Hard rule for child\n- Children are leaves. If you discover work that belongs in a different\n  directory, do NOT call /refocus. Surface it in Result.suggested_follow_ups\n  for the parent to decide.\n\n## Pointer back\n- Source session: `~/.claude/projects/-home-administrator-projects-aws/700184f3-55a6-4052-b9fa-225f8550bc2e.jsonl`\n- Originating issue brief: `~/projects/aws/nextcloud.issue.md`, reply in `~/projects/aws/nextcloud.response.md`.\n- To resume this child's session: `cd /home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver && claude --resume 59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30`\n\n---\n\n## Result\n<empty until child writes>\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":90,"oldLines":4,"newStart":90,"newLines":62,"lines":[" ---"," "," ## Result","-<empty until child writes>","+","+**Status**: completed","+","+**Definition-of-Done met**","+- ✓ `docker exec mailserver openssl x509 -in /etc/dms/tls/cert -noout -ext subjectAltName` → `DNS:*.ai-servicers.com, DNS:ai-servicers.com`.","+- ✓ Peer-verified TLS to `mail.ai-servicers.com:993` succeeds — checked with hostname","+  verification actually enabled (`-verify_hostname mail.ai-servicers.com`, not just chain","+  trust), and a negative control (`-verify_hostname nope.example.com`) confirmed the flag","+  rejects a mismatched name, proving the positive check was real. Also confirmed SMTP 587","+  (`Verified peername: *.ai-servicers.com`) since Nextcloud Mail needs both.","+- ✓ `mailserver` and `mail-edge-wg` both `healthy` after restarting only `mailserver` (per the","+  brief's gotcha, `mail-edge-wg` was left untouched). Port 25 through the edge answers","+  `220 mail.ai-servicers.com ESMTP`.","+- ✓ Change and both gotchas recorded in `CLAUDE.md` (SSL Configuration section + an update","+  note under Integration with Nextcloud).","+","+**Summary**","+`mailserver`'s cert bind mount pointed at Traefik's apex-only `ai-servicers.com` cert dir","+(SAN `ai-servicers.com` only). Repointed it at the wildcard dir","+(`*.ai-servicers.com`, SAN `*.ai-servicers.com, ai-servicers.com`) in `docker-compose.yml`,","+quoted for YAML safety per the brief's glob-character gotcha. Restarted only `mailserver`;","+both containers came back healthy. Verified with a genuine hostname-verifying TLS handshake","+(not just chain trust) against the public edge IP with SNI `mail.ai-servicers.com`, on both","+993 and 587. Traefik's cert extraction was untouched, confirming the brief's diagnosis that","+it was never at fault.","+","+**Artifacts produced**","+- `docker-compose.yml` — cert bind-mount source changed to the wildcard directory.","+- `CLAUDE.md` — SSL Configuration section rewritten with the fix, rationale, and both","+  gotchas (glob-char directory name; traefik-certs dir is write-denied, inspect read-only via","+  `docker exec`); Nextcloud integration section updated with a 2026-07-28 note distinguishing","+  this (now-fixed) cert blocker from the still-open Traefik LAN routing regression.","+- Commit `34ba745` on `main`, pushed to `origin/main`.","+","+**Suggested follow-ups (parent decides)**","+- Divergent uncommitted WIP was found already in this working tree at start of session,","+  unrelated to this brief, and deliberately left untouched (staged only my own hunks via","+  `git add -p`): a `192.168.1.13:143:143` port mapping on `mail-edge-wg` in","+  `docker-compose.yml`, and catch-all aliases in `config/postfix-virtual.cf`","+  (`@ai-servicers.com`, `hello@ai-servicers.com` → `websurfinmurf@ai-servicers.com`). These","+  look like leftover work from the sibling `2026-07-28-proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077` session","+  (its `.worker.log` is also modified, uncommitted). Because I recreated `mailserver` via","+  `docker compose up -d mailserver`, it re-read the bind-mounted `./config`, so the","+  uncommitted `postfix-virtual.cf` aliases (including the `@ai-servicers.com` catch-all) are","+  now **live in the running Postfix**, uncommitted, with MX pointing at this server. The","+  `proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077` session (or its parent) should review and commit or discard","+  this WIP.","+- Untracked `docker-compose.yml.bak-lan143` in the repo root — appears to be a manual backup","+  from other WIP, not mine; left alone.","+- The still-open Traefik LAN TCP-routing regression (`mail.ai-servicers.com:993` via","+  `192.168.1.13` returns `HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request`) is unrelated to this fix and remains a","+  Traefik-project change, per existing CLAUDE.md.","+","+**Material changes (for /context-save)**","+- `docs/context/security.md` (or equivalent): the mail TLS certificate source changed from","+  the apex-only Traefik-dumped dir to the wildcard dir, fixing SAN validation for","+  `mail.ai-servicers.com` — update if a canonical cert-path fact lives there.","+- No architecture-level change (same cert source, same dumper, same container topology) —","+  primarily a bind-mount source correction."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
