{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /home/administrator/.claude/skills/claude-shared/skills/context-save\n\n# Context Save\n\nMaintain persistent, terse project knowledge in `docs/context/` for AI agent continuity across sessions.\n\n**Design goal**: If the code got deleted but these files survived, an AI should reconstruct ~75% of the application in one shot.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- **Automatically (context-loss boundaries)**: Stop, SubagentStop, PreCompact, SessionEnd, and `UserPromptSubmit` matching `/clear|/compact|/exit|/quit` all fire `context-save-check.sh` or `context-save-on-prompt.sh`. These nudge — and in high-pressure cases **block** — until decisions and lessons are captured.\n- **Manually**: `/context-save` to update context files after work\n- **Bootstrap**: `/context-save init` to scaffold `docs/context/` for a new project\n\n### Hook escalation tiers (`context-save-check.sh`)\n\nContext pressure is proxied by transcript file size (`transcript_path` in the hook payload). `PreCompact` events get bumped one tier because the next compaction will lose detail regardless.\n\n| Signal | Pressure | Behavior |\n|---|---|---|\n| `docs/context/` already touched | any | Soft reminder + checklist, no escalation |\n| Code changed > 15 diff lines, docs/context/ untouched, pressure **high** or **critical** | high+ | **Blocks stop** via `{\"decision\":\"block\",\"reason\":...}` — agent must save before truly stopping |\n| Code changed > 15 diff lines, docs/context/ untouched | low/medium | Strong reminder naming the 8 files |\n| Minor code changes only | any | Soft reminder |\n| No code changes (decision-only session) | any | Checklist only |\n\n### Hook escalation (`context-save-on-prompt.sh`, `UserPromptSubmit`)\n\nFires when the user types `/clear`, `/compact`, `/exit`, or `/quit`:\n\n- **Significant unsaved code changes** (>15 diff lines, no `docs/context/` updates, project has `docs/context/`) → **blocks the prompt** with the checklist; user must resubmit after saves complete.\n- **Otherwise** → injects the checklist as additional context; prompt proceeds.\n\n### Decisions & lessons checklist (always injected)\n\nEvery hook fire surfaces the same routing checklist so capture is automatic in intent, not just at stop:\n\n  (a) **Decisions** (architecture, approach, tradeoffs) → `docs/context/architecture.md` or `requirements.md`\n  (b) **Lessons / gotchas**\n        - project-specific → `agent-memory write --memory-kind gotcha --subject \"<topic>\" \"<lesson>\"` (or `docs/context/gotchas.md` if no agent-memory)\n        - cross-project → `~/.claude/skills/troubleshooting/SKILL.md`\n  (c) **User corrections / preferences** → feedback memory under `~/.claude/projects/.../memory/`\n  (d) **Code/config changes** that move architecture, interfaces, security, or operations → matching `docs/context/` file\n\n## Files\n\nAll files live in `{project}/docs/context/`. **The skill ships a DEFAULT set (the 8 canonical files\nbelow); projects APPEND app-specific \"extension\" files via `CLAUDE.md` frontmatter.** Effective set =\ndefault ∪ project extensions. See \"Per-project menu\" below.\n\n### Default set (every project gets these)\n\n| # | File | Description |\n|---|------|-------------|\n| 1 | `requirements.md` | Business rules, user workflows, product constraints |\n| 2 | `architecture.md` | Components, boundaries, data flow, service topology |\n| 3 | `interfaces.md` | API contracts, schemas, entities, events, config surfaces |\n| 4 | `conventions.md` | Code patterns, naming, frameworks, libraries, module layout |\n| 5 | `security.md` | Auth, secrets, trust boundaries, access rules |\n| 6 | `operations.md` | Deployment, containers, networking, config, runtime |\n| 7 | `testing.md` | Critical paths, regression checks, coverage strategy |\n| 8 | `invariants.md` | Hard rules that must hold (anchors referenced by ADRs + tests) |\n\n### `gotchas.md` — **route to agent-memory where available**\n\nGotchas are accreting, ad-hoc observations — the wrong shape for a static reference doc. If the project has agent-memory wired (signal: project declares `context-save.gotchas_via_memory: true` in CLAUDE.md, or `agent-memory` CLI is on PATH), **write gotchas via `agent-memory write --memory-kind gotcha --subject \"<topic>\" \"<the lesson>\"`** instead of editing a markdown file.\n\nThe daily reconciler (if deployed) will promote durable gotchas into the appropriate canonical file over time.\n\nProjects without agent-memory can still keep a plain `gotchas.md`.\n\n### Per-project menu (CLAUDE.md frontmatter)\n\n**The default set (the 8 canonical files) is baked into this skill — you do NOT re-declare it.**\nProjects only declare what they ADD or override, via a YAML frontmatter block at the top of `CLAUDE.md`:\n\n```yaml\n---\ncontext-save:\n  extends: [signal-lifecycle, options-exec]   # APP-SPECIFIC files, APPENDED to the default set\n  files: [architecture, operations, invariants]  # OPTIONAL explicit override — REPLACES the default (trim)\n  gotchas_via_memory: false\n  routing:                                     # OPTIONAL: teach the skill where app content belongs\n    trading-rules: tradingrequirements.md      #   (esp. big app docs that live OUTSIDE docs/context/)\n---\n```\n\n**Effective set = default ∪ extensions.** Resolution order:\n1. Start from the **default** (canonical 8) — UNLESS `files:` is present, in which case `files:`\n   REPLACES the default (an explicit subset, for projects that want to trim it).\n2. **Append `extends:`** — project-specific files (any name), added on top. This is the RECOMMENDED\n   knob: you list only what you're ADDING, never the defaults.\n3. **Auto-discover extensions:** any `docs/context/*.md` that is NOT a canonical file is ALSO treated\n   as a project extension the skill maintains — so dropping in `docs/context/<name>.md` is enough to\n   adopt it (still list it in `extends:` for discoverability).\n\nKeys:\n- `extends` — app-specific context files appended to the default. **This is the customization point.**\n- `files` — OPTIONAL explicit override of the default (a subset). Omit to keep all 8 defaults.\n- `gotchas_via_memory` — true routes gotchas to `agent-memory`; false keeps a local `gotchas.md`.\n- `routing` — OPTIONAL `topic → file` map so app content lands in the right place, including large\n  app-specific docs kept OUTSIDE `docs/context/` (e.g. `tradingrequirements.md`).\n\n**Extension-file rules:** each extension MUST open with a one-line purpose header (`> Purpose: …`)\nso its scope is self-evident, and follows the same terse/bounded/atomic writing rules as canonical\nfiles. When routing content, ask \"which ONE file answers this?\" — canonical first, then extensions.\n\n**If the frontmatter is absent** AND `docs/context/` exists: use the default set + any auto-discovered\nextensions, and suggest `/context-save-upgrade` to make the menu explicit (one-time).\n\n## Workflow\n\n### On Hook Reminder (Stop/SubagentStop/PreCompact/SessionEnd)\n\n1. Assess what you changed during this session\n2. Determine which context files are affected\n3. Read the affected file(s)\n4. Update with terse, factual entries\n5. Use `[IMPLEMENTED]` for actual state, `[PLANNED]` for future state\n6. Stage changes for inclusion in the next commit\n7. **Test gap scan** — run the test gap assessment (see below)\n8. **Troubleshooting tips** — if you diagnosed or resolved issues this session:\n   - **Project-specific + agent-memory available** → `agent-memory write --memory-kind gotcha --subject \"<topic>\" \"<lesson>\"` (one memory per lesson — leaner, atomic)\n   - **Project-specific + no agent-memory** → `docs/context/gotchas.md` if the project's menu includes it\n   - **Broadly applicable across services** (Docker networking, iOS Safari, MCP transport, …) → `~/.claude/skills/troubleshooting/SKILL.md`\n\n### On Manual Invocation (`/context-save`)\n\n1. Read all `docs/context/` files\n2. Compare against current project state\n3. Update any stale or missing information\n4. Prune entries that are no longer relevant\n5. **Test gap scan** — run the test gap assessment (see below)\n6. **Troubleshooting tips** — same as hook workflow step 8: project-specific → `docs/context/gotchas.md`, broadly applicable → `~/.claude/skills/troubleshooting/SKILL.md`\n\n### Test Gap Assessment (runs as final step of every workflow above)\n\nAfter updating context files, assess whether this session's code changes have adequate test coverage:\n\n1. **Identify changed source files** — list every source file (not test files, not docs) that was added or modified this session\n2. **Check for corresponding test files** — for each source file, verify a `test_*.py` (or project-equivalent) exists\n3. **Scan for untested new/modified functions** — look for functions added or significantly changed that lack test coverage\n4. **Report findings** — present a summary to the user:\n\n```\n## Test Gap Scan\n- **Files changed**: bot.py, chat_handler.py\n- **Test coverage**: bot.py → tests/test_media_control.py ✓, chat_handler.py → tests/test_chat_handler.py ✗ (missing)\n- **Untested functions**: parse_media_command() new param `client_media_state` — partially covered\n- **Recommendation**: Run `/qatests` to fill gaps\n```\n\n5. **If gaps found** — ask the user: \"Test gaps detected. Run `/qatests` to fill them?\"\n6. **If user approves** (or if invoked via hook with `--auto-test` flag) — invoke `/qatests` targeting only the identified gaps, not a full project audit\n\n### On Bootstrap (`/context-save init`)\n\n1. Create `docs/context/` directory\n2. Create all 7 files from templates (see templates/ directory)\n3. Populate with known project information\n4. Stage for commit\n\n### Context-strategy integration (opt-in, per-project)\n\nIf the project participates in context-strategy v2.2+ (signal: `criticality.yml` at repo root), `context-save` extends the workflow:\n\n#### Session start\n\n1. Call the project's `inbox_count()` — now real via `agent-memory inbox-count` CLI or `from agent_memory import inbox_count` (async, returns int). The legacy `scripts/inbox_count_stub.py --project <id>` still works as a sync shim; it now reports `stub_active: false` since Phase-2 cutover (Task 2.6). Signature frozen (R10).\n2. If `count > 0`, print a one-line banner:\n   ```\n   <project_id>: N unreconciled items. Run `agent-memory inbox` to review\n     or `agent-memory inbox quick-resolve --all-forget` to clear.\n   ```\n   Phase 1: stub always returns 0; banner appends `(stub)` suffix.\n\n#### Before substantive edits (change-impact 3-question prompt)\n\nBefore editing any path matched by `criticality.yml`, surface:\n\n1. **Which invariant could this break?** — cite by anchor from `docs/context/invariants.md`.\n2. **Which adjacent modules participate?** — list the files this change touches transitively.\n3. **Which doc/test did you consult?** — cite the ADR / invariant / test run output.\n\nInject the project's PreToolUse hook output (authority preamble + invariant text + ADR anchors + `must_run_tests` list) as part of the response context. See project's `hooks/inject_context.py`.\n\n#### Authority conflict during session\n\nWhen the agent detects that a test/spec/ADR overrides a recalled memory:\n- Phase 1: no-op (no memory service yet).\n- Phase 2: call `agent_memory.override(memory_id, session_id, reason)`. Daemon applies authority-tier drop in subsequent recalls.\n\n#### Promotion helper\n\nWhen a durable learning surfaces during work (repeated decision, pattern across sessions):\n- Phase 1: log candidate to `/tmp/promotion-candidates.log` (informational).\n- Phase 2: agent-driven promotion per `docs/context-strategy/principles.md` §1 — detect + draft + auto-commit with user confirmation.\n\n#### Opt-out\n\nProjects without `criticality.yml` see zero behavior change. The 8-file default context-save workflow above is unaffected.\n\n## Writing Rules\n\n### MUST DO\n- **Terse**: Bullet points and tables. No prose paragraphs.\n- **Factual**: Only write what IS true or explicitly mark `[PLANNED]`\n- **Scoped**: Each entry belongs in exactly one file. Ask: \"which question does this answer?\"\n- **Bounded**: Each file stays under 200 lines. Prune old/low-priority entries when full.\n- **Atomic**: Each bullet point is self-contained and understandable without context.\n\n### MUST NOT DO\n- No filler, pleasantries, or narrative prose\n- No timestamps on individual entries (git history tracks this)\n- No duplicate information already in CLAUDE.md (CLAUDE.md = directives, context files = knowledge)\n- No empty sections — delete section headers with no content\n- No separate commits for context-only changes — bundle with code commits\n\n### Status Markers\n```markdown\n- [IMPLEMENTED] PostgreSQL for primary data store\n- [PLANNED] Redis cache layer for session management\n- [DEPRECATED] MongoDB connector (removed in v2)\n```\n\n### Routing Guide\nWhen unsure which file to update, ask: \"where would I look for this when reconstructing?\"\n\n- Clarified what the system must do? → `requirements.md`\n- Changed how components connect? → `architecture.md`\n- Changed API shapes, DB schema, events? → `interfaces.md`\n- Changed code patterns, libs, naming? → `conventions.md`\n- Found a security constraint? → `security.md`\n- Changed deploy/build/run process? → `operations.md`\n- Changed test strategy or found a gap? → `testing.md`\n- Discovered non-obvious behavior? → `gotchas.md`\n\n## Templates\n\nTemplates for all 8 files are in the `templates/` directory. Read them when scaffolding a new project.\n\n| Template | Load When |\n|----------|-----------|\n| `templates/requirements.md` | Scaffolding new project |\n| `templates/architecture.md` | Scaffolding new project |\n| `templates/interfaces.md` | Scaffolding new project |\n| `templates/conventions.md` | Scaffolding new project |\n| `templates/security.md` | Scaffolding new project |\n| `templates/operations.md` | Scaffolding new project |\n| `templates/testing.md` | Scaffolding new project |\n| `templates/gotchas.md` | Scaffolding new project |\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30","uuid":"a3a5c02e-188b-4fd1-adc9-7673e108e672","timestamp":"2026-07-28T22:23:08.451Z","isSynthetic":true}
