{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L95KmNLdo1fvVRgD3TFVLZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Operations\n2\t\n3\t## Restart semantics — mail-edge-wg / mailserver coupling\n4\t- [IMPLEMENTED] Both containers are `restart: unless-stopped` and start in order via\n5\t  `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` — this only orders *startup*, not ongoing recovery.\n6\t- Restarting `mail-edge-wg` alone **destroys the shared network namespace**. `mailserver`\n7\t  keeps running inside the now-orphaned netns rather than being restarted by Docker.\n8\t- `mailserver`'s healthcheck checks for a live `wg0` inside its netns (not just an open port)\n9\t  specifically to catch this — but detection ≠ recovery. **Manually restart `mailserver`**\n10\t  after any `mail-edge-wg` restart.\n11\t\n12\t## Host reboot\n13\t- [IMPLEMENTED] Both containers come back on host reboot via `restart: unless-stopped` (no\n14\t  host-level `wg-quick@wg0` systemd unit — this host has no passwordless sudo for an\n15\t  autonomous worker to install one).\n16\t\n17\t## Secrets\n18\t- `~/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` (mode 600) — WireGuard peer config, generated by\n19\t  `~/projects/aws/mail-edge/`. `AllowedIPs = 10.77.0.0/24` — scoped to the tunnel subnet only,\n20\t  so `mailserver`'s general internet egress (e.g. SendGrid relay) is unaffected.\n21\t- `~/projects/secrets/docker-mailserver.env` — main env config (unchanged by this work).\n22\t\n23\t## DKIM key material\n24\t- `config/opendkim/keys/` contains a private key readable only by `root` inside the container\n25\t  (perm-denied for the `administrator` user). [IMPLEMENTED] `.gitignore`d as `config/opendkim/`\n26\t  — never commit private key material.\n27\t\n28\t## Verification commands used\n29\t```bash\n30\tdocker logs mailserver 2>&1 | grep -i 'postscreen\\|submission.*smtpd\\|submissions.*smtpd\\|imap-login'\n31\t# real client IP (e.g. 108.35.80.85) should appear, not 10.77.0.1\n32\t```\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30","uuid":"88421f32-202c-4d58-81e5-0d8ba975d084","timestamp":"2026-07-28T22:23:17.288Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/context/operations.md","content":"# Operations\n\n## Restart semantics — mail-edge-wg / mailserver coupling\n- [IMPLEMENTED] Both containers are `restart: unless-stopped` and start in order via\n  `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` — this only orders *startup*, not ongoing recovery.\n- Restarting `mail-edge-wg` alone **destroys the shared network namespace**. `mailserver`\n  keeps running inside the now-orphaned netns rather than being restarted by Docker.\n- `mailserver`'s healthcheck checks for a live `wg0` inside its netns (not just an open port)\n  specifically to catch this — but detection ≠ recovery. **Manually restart `mailserver`**\n  after any `mail-edge-wg` restart.\n\n## Host reboot\n- [IMPLEMENTED] Both containers come back on host reboot via `restart: unless-stopped` (no\n  host-level `wg-quick@wg0` systemd unit — this host has no passwordless sudo for an\n  autonomous worker to install one).\n\n## Secrets\n- `~/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` (mode 600) — WireGuard peer config, generated by\n  `~/projects/aws/mail-edge/`. `AllowedIPs = 10.77.0.0/24` — scoped to the tunnel subnet only,\n  so `mailserver`'s general internet egress (e.g. SendGrid relay) is unaffected.\n- `~/projects/secrets/docker-mailserver.env` — main env config (unchanged by this work).\n\n## DKIM key material\n- `config/opendkim/keys/` contains a private key readable only by `root` inside the container\n  (perm-denied for the `administrator` user). [IMPLEMENTED] `.gitignore`d as `config/opendkim/`\n  — never commit private key material.\n\n## Verification commands used\n```bash\ndocker logs mailserver 2>&1 | grep -i 'postscreen\\|submission.*smtpd\\|submissions.*smtpd\\|imap-login'\n# real client IP (e.g. 108.35.80.85) should appear, not 10.77.0.1\n```\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
