{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019HA8Wfkt5XXVC1oPXR74mz","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/context/operations.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30","uuid":"51971e26-393f-4df7-8df7-7ec3ea127495","timestamp":"2026-07-28T22:23:25.817Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/context/operations.md","oldString":"## Verification commands used","newString":"## TLS certificate source\n- [IMPLEMENTED] `mailserver`'s cert bind mount points at Traefik's **wildcard** cert dir:\n  `\"/home/administrator/projects/data/traefik-certs/*.ai-servicers.com:/certs:ro\"`\n  (quoted — the dir name is literally `*.ai-servicers.com`; not a shell glob, Compose passes\n  bind-mount sources through literally, but an unquoted plain YAML scalar *starting* with `*`\n  would be parsed as a YAML alias).\n- `traefik-certs-dumper` (`file --domain-subdir` mode) writes one dir per cert under that same\n  parent, including a separate apex-only `ai-servicers.com/` dir (SAN `ai-servicers.com` only)\n  — do not point at that one. `OVERRIDE_HOSTNAME=mail.ai-servicers.com` requires the wildcard's\n  SAN (`*.ai-servicers.com, ai-servicers.com`) to pass peer-verifying clients (Nextcloud Mail).\n- The parent `traefik-certs/` dir is under `projects/data/`, hard-denied for writes by the\n  destructive-guard hook. Inspect read-only via `docker exec` into a container that already\n  mounts it (e.g. `traefik-certs-dumper`); never edit it directly.\n- Verifying the fix requires actual hostname verification, not just chain trust:\n  `openssl s_client ... -verify_hostname mail.ai-servicers.com` (not `-verify N` alone, which\n  only checks the chain and would pass identically against the wrong-SAN cert too).\n\n## Verification commands used","originalFile":"# Operations\n\n## Restart semantics — mail-edge-wg / mailserver coupling\n- [IMPLEMENTED] Both containers are `restart: unless-stopped` and start in order via\n  `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` — this only orders *startup*, not ongoing recovery.\n- Restarting `mail-edge-wg` alone **destroys the shared network namespace**. `mailserver`\n  keeps running inside the now-orphaned netns rather than being restarted by Docker.\n- `mailserver`'s healthcheck checks for a live `wg0` inside its netns (not just an open port)\n  specifically to catch this — but detection ≠ recovery. **Manually restart `mailserver`**\n  after any `mail-edge-wg` restart.\n\n## Host reboot\n- [IMPLEMENTED] Both containers come back on host reboot via `restart: unless-stopped` (no\n  host-level `wg-quick@wg0` systemd unit — this host has no passwordless sudo for an\n  autonomous worker to install one).\n\n## Secrets\n- `~/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` (mode 600) — WireGuard peer config, generated by\n  `~/projects/aws/mail-edge/`. `AllowedIPs = 10.77.0.0/24` — scoped to the tunnel subnet only,\n  so `mailserver`'s general internet egress (e.g. SendGrid relay) is unaffected.\n- `~/projects/secrets/docker-mailserver.env` — main env config (unchanged by this work).\n\n## DKIM key material\n- `config/opendkim/keys/` contains a private key readable only by `root` inside the container\n  (perm-denied for the `administrator` user). [IMPLEMENTED] `.gitignore`d as `config/opendkim/`\n  — never commit private key material.\n\n## Verification commands used\n```bash\ndocker logs mailserver 2>&1 | grep -i 'postscreen\\|submission.*smtpd\\|submissions.*smtpd\\|imap-login'\n# real client IP (e.g. 108.35.80.85) should appear, not 10.77.0.1\n```\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":6,"newStart":25,"newLines":23,"lines":["   (perm-denied for the `administrator` user). [IMPLEMENTED] `.gitignore`d as `config/opendkim/`","   — never commit private key material."," ","+## TLS certificate source","+- [IMPLEMENTED] `mailserver`'s cert bind mount points at Traefik's **wildcard** cert dir:","+  `\"/home/administrator/projects/data/traefik-certs/*.ai-servicers.com:/certs:ro\"`","+  (quoted — the dir name is literally `*.ai-servicers.com`; not a shell glob, Compose passes","+  bind-mount sources through literally, but an unquoted plain YAML scalar *starting* with `*`","+  would be parsed as a YAML alias).","+- `traefik-certs-dumper` (`file --domain-subdir` mode) writes one dir per cert under that same","+  parent, including a separate apex-only `ai-servicers.com/` dir (SAN `ai-servicers.com` only)","+  — do not point at that one. `OVERRIDE_HOSTNAME=mail.ai-servicers.com` requires the wildcard's","+  SAN (`*.ai-servicers.com, ai-servicers.com`) to pass peer-verifying clients (Nextcloud Mail).","+- The parent `traefik-certs/` dir is under `projects/data/`, hard-denied for writes by the","+  destructive-guard hook. Inspect read-only via `docker exec` into a container that already","+  mounts it (e.g. `traefik-certs-dumper`); never edit it directly.","+- Verifying the fix requires actual hostname verification, not just chain trust:","+  `openssl s_client ... -verify_hostname mail.ai-servicers.com` (not `-verify N` alone, which","+  only checks the chain and would pass identically against the wrong-SAN cert too).","+"," ## Verification commands used"," ```bash"," docker logs mailserver 2>&1 | grep -i 'postscreen\\|submission.*smtpd\\|submissions.*smtpd\\|imap-login'"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
