{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012TFnGMqByDXj5WKcunQKXh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gotchas\n2\t\n3\t- **Traefik's TCP routing to mail is dead, not just unused.** `mailserver` used to get its\n4\t  Traefik TCP routers (25/465/587/993 TLS passthrough) via Docker labels. Since it moved to\n5\t  `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg`, labels are forbidden on it (Docker rejects labels\n6\t  alongside `network_mode: service:*`), so those routers no longer exist. Confirmed:\n7\t  `openssl s_client -connect mail.ai-servicers.com:993` TLS-handshakes fine (cert is valid)\n8\t  but then gets `HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request` instead of an IMAP banner — Traefik has no matching\n9\t  router and falls through to its HTTP stack. This silently broke Nextcloud Mail's existing\n10\t  IMAP/SMTP integration. Fix belongs in the `traefik` project (new label source, or a\n11\t  file-provider TCP route pointing at `mail-edge-wg`), not here.\n12\t\n13\t- **A `mail-edge-wg` restart does not auto-recover `mailserver`.** Restarting `mail-edge-wg`\n14\t  destroys the shared network namespace; `mailserver` keeps running in the orphaned netns\n15\t  rather than getting restarted by Docker. `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` only\n16\t  orders startup, not runtime recovery. The `mailserver` healthcheck checks for a live `wg0`\n17\t  specifically to catch this, but you still have to restart `mailserver` by hand afterward.\n18\t\n19\t- **PROXY protocol must be scoped per Postfix listener, not global.** Setting\n20\t  `postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol`/`smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol` in `postfix-main.cf`\n21\t  would also apply to the internal 127.0.0.1 amavis reinjection listener, which will never\n22\t  receive a PROXY header — breaking local delivery. Scope the directives in\n23\t  `postfix-master.cf` per listener instead.\n24\t\n25\t- **DKIM private key material lives under `config/opendkim/keys/`, owned by `root` inside the\n26\t  container** — unreadable by the host `administrator` user, and `.gitignore`d\n27\t  (`config/opendkim/`). Don't try to `git add` it; it'll fail with a permission error, and it\n28\t  should never be committed anyway.\n29\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59a355ba-da00-4059-aa80-2a345be94b30","uuid":"419d0170-34f4-4e95-9049-3dada4e1828b","timestamp":"2026-07-28T22:23:29.727Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/context/gotchas.md","content":"# Gotchas\n\n- **Traefik's TCP routing to mail is dead, not just unused.** `mailserver` used to get its\n  Traefik TCP routers (25/465/587/993 TLS passthrough) via Docker labels. Since it moved to\n  `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg`, labels are forbidden on it (Docker rejects labels\n  alongside `network_mode: service:*`), so those routers no longer exist. Confirmed:\n  `openssl s_client -connect mail.ai-servicers.com:993` TLS-handshakes fine (cert is valid)\n  but then gets `HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request` instead of an IMAP banner — Traefik has no matching\n  router and falls through to its HTTP stack. This silently broke Nextcloud Mail's existing\n  IMAP/SMTP integration. Fix belongs in the `traefik` project (new label source, or a\n  file-provider TCP route pointing at `mail-edge-wg`), not here.\n\n- **A `mail-edge-wg` restart does not auto-recover `mailserver`.** Restarting `mail-edge-wg`\n  destroys the shared network namespace; `mailserver` keeps running in the orphaned netns\n  rather than getting restarted by Docker. `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` only\n  orders startup, not runtime recovery. The `mailserver` healthcheck checks for a live `wg0`\n  specifically to catch this, but you still have to restart `mailserver` by hand afterward.\n\n- **PROXY protocol must be scoped per Postfix listener, not global.** Setting\n  `postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol`/`smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol` in `postfix-main.cf`\n  would also apply to the internal 127.0.0.1 amavis reinjection listener, which will never\n  receive a PROXY header — breaking local delivery. Scope the directives in\n  `postfix-master.cf` per listener instead.\n\n- **DKIM private key material lives under `config/opendkim/keys/`, owned by `root` inside the\n  container** — unreadable by the host `administrator` user, and `.gitignore`d\n  (`config/opendkim/`). Don't try to `git add` it; it'll fail with a permission error, and it\n  should never be committed anyway.\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}}}
